                                "sense_id": "fd23554a-67f8-3657-830f-e8ab39203f18",
                                "text": "Spanish was the only \"foreign\" language taught in the school, where most of the students spoke Spanish as a first language, and it was taught by an Anglo teacher from textbooks written by and for Anglos […] Somehow, the school administration saw no contradiction in rewarding Anglo students for learning to conjugate ser while punishing Chicano students for speaking Spanish on the school grounds."
